            <article class="lrow" id="r1" data-rank="1" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Cozy Atmosphere">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">1</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/EFxJ2RSTVtMwcv1cidCz7Q/l.jpg" alt="Curry Gate 2" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/curry-gate-south-blvd-charlotte-2?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Curry Gate 2 photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Curry Gate 2</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Indian &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 8.1 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>8.1</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Charlotte&#039;s Indian restaurant count has grown alongside the city&#039;s South Asian professional community, and Curry Gate 2 sits in that everyday tier: a moderately priced room that covers both Indian standards and Nepali cooking, which is still a short list in the 704.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Butter Chicken</span><span class="pl">Chicken Biryani</span><span class="pl">Vegetable Momos</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7049104038">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.160635%2C-80.876502" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Curry Gate 2"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Indian and Nepali Cooking, Honest Prices</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Butter Chicken</b><p>The kitchen&#039;s rich tomato-cream curry, milder than the tikka masala and best for those easing into the menu.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Chicken Biryani</b><p>Biryani arrives in generous portions, the rice volume a recurring note among regulars who order delivery.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Vegetable Momos</b><p>Steamed dumplings that signal the Nepali side of a menu that stretches well beyond standard Indian fare.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Charlotte's Indian restaurant count has grown alongside the city's South Asian professional community, and Curry Gate 2 sits in that everyday tier: a moderately priced room that covers both Indian standards and Nepali cooking, which is still a short list in the 704. The Nepali side of the menu is the more distinctive half. Vegetable momos turn up as a signature, and the kitchen's reach into that tradition gives the place a different profile than a straight-subcontinental curry house. The Indian anchor dishes, butter chicken and chicken biryani, are the volume workhorses. The biryani arrives in generous portions; rice quantity is not a complaint anyone has made here.</p>
<p>Butter chicken draws mixed readings: some find it satisfying, others pull the tikka preparation instead and find more to work with there. That split is useful information about where the kitchen is most confident. The chicken tikka reads as the stronger order when the two are set side by side. Service is consistently described as attentive and friendly, which matters in a room at this price point where the margins on hospitality are real. The packaging holds up on delivery, which suggests the kitchen takes the off-premises order seriously, not as an afterthought.</p>
<p>Pricing sits in a range that makes sense for a family dinner or a casual weeknight, and the portions trend large enough that two dishes between two people is a workable plan. There is no Nepali-Indian crossover room with a long footprint in Charlotte; the city's food scene is young enough that this combination still registers as worth noting. Curry Gate 2 is not an expense-account destination, but it is a consistent neighborhood option for South Asian cooking at a fair price.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.160635%2C-80.876502" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Curry Gate 2"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/599.webp" alt="Map showing Curry Gate 2" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Daily: 12:00 PM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>5516 South Blvd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7049104038">(704) 910-4038</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Order the chicken tikka over the butter chicken if spice and flavor depth are the priority. The momos are the reason to come if Nepali cooking is the draw.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="featwrap" data-after="r1"><div class="promotion-block promotion-ad promotion-hu promotion-hu-trow"><span class="promotion-label">Advertisement</span><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/hu/hu.css?v=1790066202"><aside class="v6-feat v6-feat--hu v6-feat--hu-row"><div class="hu-box hu-box--mrfear"><a class="hu-mrfear" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/u-mrfear/?z=list-inline-1" target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener" aria-label="Mr. Fear. Explore local Halloween guides. Opens in a new tab."><img class="art" src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/hu/halloween.webp" alt=""><span class="shade"></span><span class="brand">MR. FEAR</span><span class="season">HALLOWEEN 2026</span><span class="label">AD</span><span class="huh"><span>PLAN YOUR</span> <span class="orange">HALLOWEEN</span> <span>NIGHT.</span></span><p class="sub">Haunted houses &amp; local events.</p><span class="cta"><span class="full">Explore the guides</span><span class="short">View guides</span> <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>
</div></aside></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r2" data-rank="2" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Hidden Gem|Modern Setting|Upscale Dining">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">2</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/exlmHqa1RgAAkAZKbFuCAg/l.jpg" alt="Yunta Nikkei" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/yunta-nikkei-charlotte-2?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Yunta Nikkei photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Yunta Nikkei</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Peruvian &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 8.1 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>8.1</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Nikkei cuisine, the culinary marriage of Peruvian tradition and Japanese technique forged by the Japanese diaspora in Lima, is not a concept Charlotte has had much occasion to explore.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Nikkei Ceviche</span><span class="pl">Anticuchos Skewers</span><span class="pl">Peruvian-Style Sushi Rolls</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/yunta-nikkei/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9804952253">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.20658065698936%2C-80.86091370364267" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Yunta Nikkei"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Peruvian-Japanese Fusion With Real Conviction</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Nikkei Ceviche</b><p>The ceviche here reflects the Nikkei tradition of Peruvian-Japanese fusion, where citrus-cured fish meets Japanese precision in the prep.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Anticuchos Skewers</b><p>Anticuchos land as the heart-meat skewer classic of Lima street cooking, grilled and seasoned in the tradition the Nikkei style builds on.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Peruvian-Style Sushi Rolls</b><p>Sushi rolls reinterpreted through a Peruvian lens, the kitchen&#039;s point where Japanese technique meets South American ingredient logic most directly.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Nikkei cuisine, the culinary marriage of Peruvian tradition and Japanese technique forged by the Japanese diaspora in Lima, is not a concept Charlotte has had much occasion to explore. Yunta makes the case for it plainly. The room runs upscale without the expense-account stiffness, and the staff carries enough knowledge of the menu to guide a first-timer through a cuisine that rewards some orientation.</p>
<p>The Nikkei Ceviche anchors the menu and illustrates the kitchen's central argument: the clean acid and ají-heat of Peruvian leche de tigre applied to fish handled with Japanese precision. Portions run generous, which matters at a moderately priced room where the ticket can feel like a commitment. The Anticuchos Skewers, the grilled-heart tradition of Lima's street corners, demonstrate that the kitchen is not softening the cuisine for a North American audience. The Peruvian-Style Sushi Rolls pull both halves of the menu together, the rice and nori structure of Japan wrapped around the flavor logic of the Andes and the Pacific coast.</p>
<p>Charlotte's food scene is young, transplant-built, and still assembling its range. The Central Avenue corridor east of Plaza Midwood carries much of the city's Latin American and pan-Asian dining, and Yunta fits the broader story of that strip adding complexity and ambition. A room doing serious Nikkei work at a moderate price point is not a common thing in the 704, and the level of care the staff extends to explaining the menu suggests the kitchen knows the cuisine needs an advocate as much as a cook.</p>
<p>This is a date-night room or a table for friends willing to order broadly and compare notes. Going narrow on the menu here would miss the point.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.20658065698936%2C-80.86091370364267" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Yunta Nikkei"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/468.webp" alt="Map showing Yunta Nikkei" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 4:00 PM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Fri: 12:00 PM - 11:00 PM</b><b>Sat: 11:00 AM - 11:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>2201 S Blvd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:9804952253">(980) 495-2253</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Order across the menu rather than anchoring to one protein. The ceviche sets the kitchen&#039;s baseline, but the anticuchos and the Peruvian-style rolls together give a fuller picture of what Nikkei actually means on the plate.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r2"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-ramen-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/best-ramen-charlotte-hero-300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Ramen in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Yamazaru</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-romantic-restaurants-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/hero-best-romantic-restaurants-henderson-1-300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Romantic Restaurants in Charlotte</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Catalina Kitchen And Bar</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r3" data-rank="3" data-hood="Matthews" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Casual Vibes">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">3</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/kFYKGPIXCR_n9xQSzZ9lMQ/l.jpg" alt="Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/kabab-je-rotisserie-and-grille-matthews?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Lebanese &middot; Matthews &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.9 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.9</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Matthews is not where the Charlotte dining conversation usually lands. The food-media attention goes to NoDa, Plaza Midwood, South End; the suburbs get less scrutiny and, often, less ambition.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Mixed Grill Platter</span><span class="pl">Rotisserie Chicken</span><span class="pl">Lamb Kebabs</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7048450707">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.1281898%2C-80.7022409" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Matthews gets a serious Lebanese rotisserie</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Mixed Grill Platter</b><p>The mixed grill platter is the range-finder order, bringing together the room&#039;s kebabs and grilled meats on one plate with vegetables and dips.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Rotisserie Chicken</b><p>Rotisserie chicken is the workhorse of a Lebanese grill and the standard by which a rotisserie operation earns its name.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Lamb Kebabs</b><p>Lamb kebabs are the signature protein at a room like this, where the quality of the grind and the seasoning do the talking.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Matthews is not where the Charlotte dining conversation usually lands. The food-media attention goes to NoDa, Plaza Midwood, South End; the suburbs get less scrutiny and, often, less ambition. Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille is the kind of room that makes that geographic bias look lazy. It is a moderately priced Lebanese kitchen in a suburb southeast of Mecklenburg, and it is doing the work with care.</p>
<p>The mixed grill platter is the clearest statement of what the kitchen is after: beef and lamb kabobs that arrive cooked through without losing their juice, paired with grilled vegetables that hold some snap rather than collapsing into softness. That combination of doneness and texture is not accidental; it is the basic discipline that separates a serious kebab operation from a perfunctory one. The lamb kebabs on their own reinforce the point. The rotisserie chicken is the other anchor of the menu, straightforward by design, and the dips alongside the meats pull their weight.</p>
<p>The cauliflower appetizer is worth separate attention. It comes out tender inside and crisped at the edges, seasoned with enough conviction that it reads as a dish rather than a side thought. In a meat-forward menu, a vegetable preparation that earns that kind of notice says something about how the kitchen is running.</p>
<p>The room does not position itself as a special-occasion destination. Service moves at speed, the format is casual, and the approach is plainly family-friendly. The price sits at the moderate register, which in the Matthews context means this is the neighborhood's everyday Lebanese option rather than an event. Charlotte's food scene was built, a lease at a time, by rooms exactly like this one: not Uptown, not the boom neighborhoods, just a kitchen doing its cuisine with enough consistency that the surrounding community keeps returning. Kabab-Je fits that pattern.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.1281898%2C-80.7022409" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/386.webp" alt="Map showing Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon: Closed</b><b>Tue - Sun: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>2233 Matthews Township Pkwy</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7048450707">(704) 845-0707</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The cauliflower appetizer is the sleeper order; get it alongside the mixed grill platter. The room moves at speed, so this is a reliable weeknight table rather than a long-reservation evening.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r3"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="Related"><span class="promotion-label">Related</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-matthews/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-matthews-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Matthews (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Kabab-Je Rotisserie &amp; Grille</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-bbq-charlotte-smoky-local-favorites/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-bbq-in-charlotte-10-smoky-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best BBQ in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Midwood Smokehouse</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r4" data-rank="4" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Casual Vibes">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">4</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/1c/d2/df/9e/logo.jpg" alt="Ace No 3 - Belmont Village" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Ace No 3 - Belmont Village photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Ace No 3 - Belmont Village</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Burgers &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.8 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.8</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Ace No 3 in Belmont Village is a compact, order-and-eat burger counter that keeps its proposition simple: smash burgers, a tight menu, and counter service that moves.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Ace Burger with Special Sauce</span><span class="pl">Truffle Parmesan Fries</span><span class="pl">BBQ Bacon Cheeseburger</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7049102200">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.22792%2C-80.82091" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Ace No 3 - Belmont Village"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Smash Burgers Worth the Parking Hunt</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Ace Burger with Special Sauce</b><p>The house smash burger, finished with the restaurant&#039;s own special sauce, is the anchor of the menu and the reason most first-timers come through.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Truffle Parmesan Fries</b><p>Fries cut for the parmesan-and-truffle treatment, a side that holds its own against the burger lineup.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>BBQ Bacon Cheeseburger</b><p>The BBQ bacon cheeseburger layers smoked-sweet barbecue sauce with bacon and cheese on the same smash-style patty that defines the kitchen.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Ace No 3 in Belmont Village is a compact, order-and-eat burger counter that keeps its proposition simple: smash burgers, a tight menu, and counter service that moves. The room is small enough that the three parking spots out back tell the whole story of its scale. Come early or order online; the operation is built for efficiency, not lingering.</p>
<p>The Ace Burger with Special Sauce is the signature, a straightforward smash-style patty where the sear does the work and the house sauce ties it together. The BBQ Bacon Cheeseburger leans into the same format with a bolder build, and the Truffle Parmesan Fries are the side worth ordering specifically, distinct enough from standard fries to justify the mention. The build-your-own option lets regulars customize without overcomplicating the kitchen's output, which is a sensible approach for a counter-service room running at volume. Seasoning on the patties runs assertive, which lands well for some and reads as oversalted for others; that's the honest note from the record.</p>
<p>Charlotte has no shortage of burger spots riding the smash-patty wave, and Ace No 3 sits in that category without pretense. The price point is moderate, the format is casual, and the crowd trends toward families and regulars who already know the order. It fits the Belmont Village neighborhood's everyday-eats register: not a destination room, but a reliable local option that earns its repeat business through consistency rather than spectacle. For a city still assembling its dining identity one lease at a time, the corner burger counter that just works has its own honest value.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.22792%2C-80.82091" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Ace No 3 - Belmont Village"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/471.webp" alt="Map showing Ace No 3 - Belmont Village" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1001 Belmont Ave</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7049102200">(704) 910-2200</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Order online before arrival to avoid the parking crunch at the small lot behind the building. The Truffle Parmesan Fries are the side to get; the Ace Burger with Special Sauce is the cleaner choice if heavy seasoning is a concern.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r4"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="Related"><span class="promotion-label">Related</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-burgers-charlotte-local-favorites/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-burgers-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Burgers Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Pinky&#x27;s Westside Grill</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-date-night-restaurants-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/best-date-night-restaurants-in-las-vegas-2026-300x201.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Date Night Restaurants in Charlotte</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Yunta Nikkei</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r5" data-rank="5" data-hood="Concord" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Casual Vibes">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">5</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/erQ7JPgBEaxpDQmmaqaOYg/l.jpg" alt="The Smoke Pit" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/the-smoke-pit-concord?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="The Smoke Pit photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">The Smoke Pit</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">BBQ &middot; Concord &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.7 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.7</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">The Smoke Pit sits in Concord, out in Cabarrus County where the Speedway money and the old mill towns overlap, and it operates as the kind of room that earns its local-favorite status without announcing it.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Smoked Brisket Platter</span><span class="pl">BBQ Ribs</span><span class="pl">Pulled Pork Sandwich</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7047957573">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.4219625%2C-80.61465612331828" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for The Smoke Pit"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Concord&#039;s Barbecue Room That Travels Well</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Smoked Brisket Platter</b><p>The anchor of the menu: thick-sliced smoked brisket with rich bark, served as a full platter built for serious portions.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>BBQ Ribs</b><p>The ribs draw comparisons to the best the region offers, a strong argument for this Concord spot in any broader Carolina BBQ conversation.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Pulled Pork Sandwich</b><p>Pulled pork on a sandwich, the Piedmont standard done with the kind of smoke depth that holds up against far better-known rooms.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>The Smoke Pit sits in Concord, out in Cabarrus County where the Speedway money and the old mill towns overlap, and it operates as the kind of room that earns its local-favorite status without announcing it. The food is the argument: smoked brisket platters with the kind of rich, layered flavor that holds up against a lifetime of regional comparisons, ribs that have drawn visitors arriving from the coasts with serious barbecue credentials, and a pulled pork sandwich that makes the case for the Piedmont tradition without needing to lecture about it. Charlotte sits in Lexington-style territory, chopped pork shoulder and a tomato-vinegar red dip, and The Smoke Pit works that regional thread alongside the Texas-brisket influence that has moved into the metro over the last decade.</p>
<p>Both coexist here without apology. Portions run generous, a fact the record confirms repeatedly, so the moderately priced entry point represents real value rather than just positioning. The catering operation is a meaningful part of the business, with event logistics that hold up under the pressure of large-scale service, a signal that the kitchen can execute at volume without the food suffering.</p>
<p>For visitors to the 704 from elsewhere in the country, this room tends to recalibrate expectations about what the Carolina Piedmont can do with smoke and time. The room itself reads casual and family-friendly, the kind of place where a weeknight dinner and a wedding catering contract occupy the same operation. In a region where barbecue identity is still being negotiated between the Lexington tradition and the national brisket wave, The Smoke Pit holds a confident position.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.4219625%2C-80.61465612331828" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to The Smoke Pit"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/360.webp" alt="Map showing The Smoke Pit" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Sat: 11:00 AM - 8:00 PM</b><b>Sun: Closed</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>796 Concord Pkwy N</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7047957573">(704) 795-7573</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The ribs are the order that converts skeptics; first-timers from out of town who think they know barbecue tend to reconsider after a rack here. Portions run large, so a platter handles more than one appetite if the table wants variety.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
