        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">6</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/08/6b/a4/df/the-cellar-at-duckworth.jpg" alt="The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Gastropubs &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.7 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.7</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Charlotte&#039;s gastropub scene leans casual by default, which makes a room like The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s worth noting.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Truffle Mac and Cheese</span><span class="pl">Beer-Braised Short Ribs</span><span class="pl">Gourmet Burger</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/the-cellar-at-duckworths/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9803494078">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.22924%2C-80.83971" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Below Street Level, Above the Noise</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Truffle Mac and Cheese</b><p>The truffle mac anchors the comfort side of this gastropub menu, rich enough to hold its own as a standalone order.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Beer-Braised Short Ribs</b><p>Beer-braised short ribs represent the kitchen&#039;s longer-cook ambitions, the kind of dish that signals a gastropub taking the food as seriously as the taps.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Gourmet Burger</b><p>The gourmet burger is the reliable centerpiece here, the order for anyone who wants craft-bar quality without committing to a full dinner program.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Charlotte's gastropub scene leans casual by default, which makes a room like The Cellar at Duckworth's worth noting. The concept is upscale British-American gastropub, but the execution reads as something more considered than that label usually suggests. Operating below street level, the room runs small and deliberate: reservations are the sensible move, particularly around holidays, and the kitchen fires at a pace that rewards patience over a quick turn. The space stays lively despite its scale, and the service record holds up across a crowd that arrives for occasions rather than impulse.</p>
<p>The signature dishes say something about the kitchen's priorities. The truffle mac and cheese is the kind of dish that gets reordered, which in a small room with a focused menu signals something consistent in the execution. Beer-braised short ribs are the logical anchor: long-cooked, pub-rooted, and the sort of thing a well-run bar kitchen either does very well or reveals itself by. The gourmet burger rounds out a three-point menu strategy that hedges upward without losing the gastropub identity. Lamb chops also register prominently, pointing to a kitchen willing to carry a protein that asks more of its sourcing and prep.</p>
<p>The price point is upscale without reaching fine dining, which positions this room for business dinners that do not require white tablecloths and for date nights where the mood matters as much as the food. The banking-crowd clientele that drives a lot of SouthPark and Uptown dining has a version of this room everywhere; what separates the Cellar is the character that comes from a below-grade space and a menu that trusts the quality of its ingredients over volume.</p>
<p>For Charlotte, a city that built its independent dining scene in the last two decades largely by iteration, a gastropub that runs small and runs consistent is its own argument.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.22924%2C-80.83971" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/361.webp" alt="Map showing The Cellar at Duckworth&#039;s" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Wed: 4:00 PM - 11:00 PM</b><b>Thu - Sat: 4:00 PM - 12:00 AM</b><b>Sun: 4:00 PM - 11:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>330 N Tryon St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:9803494078">(980) 349-4078</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Reserve ahead, especially on weekends or any holiday evening; the room fills and does not turn quickly. The lamb chops and the truffle mac and cheese together read as the strongest double order on the menu.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r6"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-italian-food-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-italian-food-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Italian Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Mama Ricotta&#x27;s</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-delis-charlotte-local-favorites/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-delis-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Delis Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> The Common Market</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r7" data-rank="7" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Romantic Spot|Local Favorite">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">7</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0f/a4/6a/77/historic-1913-bungalow.jpg" alt="The Fig Tree Restaurant" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="The Fig Tree Restaurant photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">The Fig Tree Restaurant</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">New American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.5 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.5</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">The Fig Tree Restaurant operates in the register Charlotte&#039;s banking-boom brought to town: special-occasion upscale, the kind of room where the food is expected to carry the weight of the evening.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Duck Breast with Cherry Gastrique</span><span class="pl">House-Made Lobster Ravioli</span><span class="pl">Herb-Crusted Rack of Lamb</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/the-fig-tree-restaurant/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043323322">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.21657923041921%2C-80.82263478628032" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for The Fig Tree Restaurant"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Charlotte&#039;s Special-Occasion Room, Earned</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Duck Breast with Cherry Gastrique</b><p>The kitchen&#039;s signature pairing of pan-seared duck breast against a cherry gastrique anchors the menu&#039;s richer, more composed side.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>House-Made Lobster Ravioli</b><p>House-made pasta folded around lobster is the kind of preparation that signals where a kitchen puts its craft.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Herb-Crusted Rack of Lamb</b><p>Rack of lamb with an herb crust holds the menu&#039;s top tier, suited to the room&#039;s polished, special-occasion register.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>The Fig Tree Restaurant operates in the register Charlotte's banking-boom brought to town: special-occasion upscale, the kind of room where the food is expected to carry the weight of the evening. The kitchen does not waste the opportunity. The signature dishes span duck, lamb, and lobster ravioli, and the menu reaches further into grilled octopus roasted with Poblano peppers, fingerling potatoes, and grape tomatoes, and escargot. That range signals a kitchen running a full program rather than coasting on a single marquee protein. The pan-seared duck breast with cherry gastrique sits at the center of what the kitchen does best: classical French technique applied to American fine-dining expectations. The herb-crusted rack of lamb and the house-made lobster ravioli hold to the same standard, scratch preparations at a price point that assumes the occasion justifies it. The sea bass draws repeat attention as well, landing closer to the everyday-elegant end of the menu.</p>
<p>The room has an outdoor section that functions well on a good Carolina evening, and the patio experience reads as the more relaxed of the two options. Inside, the quiet runs formal to the point of stiff for some guests, the kind of stillness that works for a proposal but can feel pressured on a first date. The menu is labeled for dietary accommodations including gluten-free items, a practical detail that signals attentiveness to the table rather than mere menu polish. Charlotte did not have rooms like this in the 1980s; it built them alongside the banking corridors and the SouthPark money. The Fig Tree fits that lineage: not a transplanted national concept, but a local room that took the upscale occasion-dining assignment seriously and has held its footing.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.21657923041921%2C-80.82263478628032" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to The Fig Tree Restaurant"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/427.webp" alt="Map showing The Fig Tree Restaurant" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Fri: 5:30 PM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sat: 5:00 PM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 5:00 PM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1601 E 7th St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043323322">(704) 332-3322</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The outdoor seating is the call on a clear night; the patio loosens the room&#039;s formality without sacrificing the kitchen&#039;s output. The grilled octopus is the underrated first course, a more interesting opening than the menu&#039;s classical anchors.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r7"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="Related"><span class="promotion-label">Related</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-new-american-restaurants-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-new-american-restaurants-in-charlotte-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best New American Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> The Fig Tree Restaurant</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-latin-american-restaurants-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-latin-american-food-in-charlotte-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Latin American Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Sabor Latin Street Grill</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r8" data-rank="8" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Romantic Spot|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">8</span>
