          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Fin &amp; Fino photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Fin &amp; Fino</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Seafood &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.5 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.5</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Charlotte&#039;s expense-account dining tends toward steakhouses, so a room that puts serious seafood at the center of a special-occasion menu is worth noting.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Halibut</span><span class="pl">Lobster Risotto</span><span class="pl">Crudo Platter</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/fin-fino/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7048005680">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.224332%2C-80.848423" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details" open>
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Fin &amp; Fino"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Uptown Seafood Built for the Occasion</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Halibut</b><p>The pan-seared halibut anchors the menu as the kitchen&#039;s cleanest argument for fresh, simply executed fish.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Lobster Risotto</b><p>Lobster risotto draws repeated visits and sits at the richer end of a menu that ranges widely in weight and approach.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Crudo Platter</b><p>The crudo platter is the place to start, offering the clearest read on how the kitchen handles raw seafood.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Charlotte's expense-account dining tends toward steakhouses, so a room that puts serious seafood at the center of a special-occasion menu is worth noting. Fin &amp; Fino operates in that upscale lane: the kind of place the banking crowd books for a milestone dinner and where the kitchen's ambitions show up in the prix-fixe format as much as in the à la carte selections.</p>
<p>The pan-seared halibut is the dish that establishes what the kitchen is after: clean technique, a fish that reads as market-fresh, executed without the distraction of heavy sauce. Alongside it, the lobster risotto represents the other register the room works in, richer and more deliberate, the sort of dish that turns a weeknight into an event. The crudo platter marks the menu's most direct claim on modern seafood cooking, raw preparations that live or die on sourcing, and the range on offer signals a kitchen that takes the program seriously.</p>
<p>The chef's tasting experience is the fullest expression of what the room is building toward: a structured, multi-course format that gives the kitchen room to move and gives the table a reason to stay. Service across both casual visits and larger parties has run competent and attentive, which matters in a room priced at this level. Charlotte's food scene is young enough that a polished full-service seafood room in this register is still a relative rarity; the city's fine-dining infrastructure leans heavily on national concepts and steakhouse formats, and a kitchen committed to seafood execution at this pitch occupies a distinct position.</p>
<p>The room skews toward date nights and celebrations rather than everyday dining, and the price reflects that. For the 704, it fills a gap that has long been underserved.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
