                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1957 E 7th St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7049190104">(704) 919-0104</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The craft Old Fashioned is the drink to open with; the pan-seared duck breast is the plate that justifies calling this dinner rather than just drinks. Tomahawk Tuesday draws a specific crowd, so plan accordingly if a quieter night is the goal.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r11"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-fine-dining-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/best-fine-dining-charlotte-hero-300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Fine Dining in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Midwood Smokehouse</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-chinese-food-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-chinese-food-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Chinese Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Kung Foo Noodle</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r12" data-rank="12" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Modern Setting|Romantic Spot">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">12</span>
