          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Sixty Vines photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Sixty Vines</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">New American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.5 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.5</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Sixty Vines is built around the wine list first and the kitchen second, which is an honest organizing principle for an upscale Charlotte room chasing the expense-account and date-night crowd.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Wood-Fired Margherita Pizza</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Salmon</span><span class="pl">Braised Short Rib</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/sixty-vines/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9802960381">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2198486%2C-80.8538232" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Sixty Vines"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Wine Program Anchors a Polished Date-Night Room</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Wood-Fired Margherita Pizza</b><p>The wood-fired Margherita anchors the pizza program here, a straightforward test of the oven that the kitchen passes.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Salmon</b><p>Pan-seared salmon sits in the reliable center of the menu, the safe call for a table split between wine-bar plates and something more substantial.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Braised Short Rib</b><p>The braised short rib is the room&#039;s serious dish, the one that earns Sixty Vines its place in Charlotte&#039;s business-dinner rotation.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Sixty Vines is built around the wine list first and the kitchen second, which is an honest organizing principle for an upscale Charlotte room chasing the expense-account and date-night crowd. The beverage program runs deep by local standards, and the food is calibrated to hold its own alongside it rather than compete. That alignment shows in the signature dishes. The wood-fired Margherita pizza arrives with the kind of char and restraint that comes from a kitchen confident in a short, focused menu rather than one trying to cover every direction.</p>
<p>The pan-seared salmon and braised short rib round out a program that reads as New American without overclaiming it, proteins handled cleanly and plated for a room where the occasion matters as much as the plate. The room itself operates across multiple visit types. It handles large party business dinners and birthday brunch celebrations with the same service profile, which is not a given at this price point. Parties of eight and couples on a Tuesday both seem to land without friction.</p>
<p>The neighborhood context is SouthPark-adjacent upscale Charlotte, where banking-money polish and a national-concept build-out are the norm. Sixty Vines fits that register without apology. The lighting is low in the evening and the build-out is modern, and the room reads differently at brunch, when the space opens up. For a city that assembled its fine-dining tier late and leaned hard on transplant tastes to do it, a wine-forward room with consistent execution and FOH attentiveness is exactly the kind of concept the market sustains.</p>
<p>The price is upscale and the experience is priced to match. Regulars who treat it as a reliable special-occasion room are getting fair value.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2198486%2C-80.8538232" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Sixty Vines"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/507.webp" alt="Map showing Sixty Vines" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
