          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r21"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="Related"><span class="promotion-label">Related</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-concord/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-concord-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Concord (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> The Smoke Pit</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-indian-trail/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-indian-trail-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Indian Trail (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> La Unica Mexican Restaurant Indian Trail</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r22" data-rank="22" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Local Favorite|Romantic Spot">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">22</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/t15VuCzuv7E6su_DrjDp-Q/l.jpg" alt="Supperland" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/supperland-charlotte" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Supperland photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Supperland</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Southern &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.2 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.2</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Supperland operates out of a converted church, and the room earns that bones.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Dry-Aged Ribeye</span><span class="pl">Buttermilk Fried Chicken</span><span class="pl">Shrimp and Grits</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/supperland/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7048177514">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.219005983591686%2C-80.81047830955967" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Supperland"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">A Church Conversion Charlotte Actually Needed</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Dry-Aged Ribeye</b><p>The dry-aged ribeye anchors Supperland&#039;s case that Southern hospitality and serious steakhouse ambition belong in the same room.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Buttermilk Fried Chicken</b><p>Buttermilk fried chicken done in the key of a room that takes the Southern canon seriously, set inside a converted Uptown church.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Shrimp and Grits</b><p>The shrimp and grits here is the reliable measure of a Southern kitchen&#039;s intentions, and Supperland&#039;s version holds up to scrutiny.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Supperland operates out of a converted church, and the room earns that bones. The space reads as comfortably grand without performing itself into exhaustion, the kind of build-out Charlotte's banking-boom era can occasionally produce when the money goes toward architecture instead of scenery. The room doubles as a cocktail destination: Colleen Hughes took the Exceptional Cocktails honor in the inaugural MICHELIN Guide American South (2025), and the beverage program here is the reason that distinction landed. This is not incidental. The bar anchors the room's identity as much as the kitchen does.</p>
<p>On the plate, the dry-aged ribeye is the signature in the expense-account sense: a cut that signals the kitchen is working with properly treated beef and expects the table to be there for it. The buttermilk fried chicken is the other pole, new-Southern done without apology, the kind of dish that shows up on Charlotte menus because the city decided it wanted a chef-driven Southern canon and rooms like this one are where that canon gets negotiated. Shrimp and grits is the third anchor, a Lowcountry staple that has migrated inland thoroughly enough to count as the region's borrowed vocabulary.</p>
<p>The room runs full service, and the FOH polish matches the price point. Walk-ins can find a seat in the bar offshoot, which functions as a lower-commitment entry to the same kitchen. The weekend brunch buffet has drawn some skepticism on value, worth factoring into how the visit is planned. For dinner, the special-occasion framing holds: the room is priced for it, staffed for it, and built for it.</p>
<p>Charlotte did not have rooms like this in 1990. The fact that it does now, and that one of them earned a national cocktails distinction in the city's first Michelin cycle, is the honest measure of how far the scene has come.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.219005983591686%2C-80.81047830955967" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Supperland"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/453.webp" alt="Map showing Supperland" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
