      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r23"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="Related"><span class="promotion-label">Related</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-sushi-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-sushi-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Sushi in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> The Cowfish Sushi Burger Bar</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-fried-chicken-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/best-fried-chicken-charlotte-hero-300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Fried Chicken in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Haberdish</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r24" data-rank="24" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Upscale Dining|Cozy Atmosphere">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">24</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/1a/13/2a/00/outside-dining.jpg" alt="Haberdish" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Haberdish photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Haberdish</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Southern &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.0 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.0</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Haberdish sits in NoDa, the old Highland Park Mill village that became one of Charlotte&#039;s first arguments for a real dining scene.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Buttermilk Fried Chicken</span><span class="pl">Shrimp and Grits</span><span class="pl">Pork Belly Benedict</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/haberdish/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7048171084">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.246509552002%2C-80.8061065673828" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Haberdish"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">NoDa&#039;s Mill-Town Southern Kitchen Earns Its Reputation</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Buttermilk Fried Chicken</b><p>The signature of this Michelin Recommended NoDa room: Alabama-white-sauce fried chicken that earns the hype surrounding it.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Shrimp and Grits</b><p>A Southern staple executed with the seriousness the mill-village setting implies, stone-ground grits anchoring the plate.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Pork Belly Benedict</b><p>The Benedict format recast in the new-Southern register Haberdish built its reputation on, pork belly standing in where ham would.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Haberdish sits in NoDa, the old Highland Park Mill village that became one of Charlotte's first arguments for a real dining scene. Jeff Tonidandel and Jamie Brown opened it in 2016, and the Michelin Guide's 2025 Recommended designation confirmed what the neighborhood already knew: the kitchen is doing serious work inside a room that carries its industrial bones without apology.</p>
<p>The buttermilk fried chicken is the throughline. It draws the orders and sets the standard the rest of the menu has to meet. The collards that come alongside it are not an afterthought; they hold their own as a reason to come back. Shrimp and grits runs the new-Southern playbook the way it should be run, grounding a familiar Piedmont combination in careful execution rather than novelty. The Pork Belly Benedict, which reads as brunch-adjacent but crosses occasions comfortably, shows the kitchen has range beyond the fried chicken anchor.</p>
<p>Deviled eggs open a meal here in the way that a well-made starter should: straightforwardly good, no need for explanation. That register carries through the whole operation. Haberdish is moderately priced for what it delivers, which places it in the productive middle of Charlotte's dining economy: not an expense-account room, not a quick counter stop. It works as a date-night destination and as the kind of place a new transplant visits once and then keeps.</p>
<p>Charlotte did not have a dining scene worth mapping in the 1980s. NoDa built one in the LYNX era, a lease at a time, and Haberdish is one of the rooms that made the neighborhood's case most clearly. The city's first Michelin Star went to Counter- in 2025; a Recommended nod in the same guide is a different tier, but it is not a consolation. It is recognition that the work here holds up against a national standard.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.246509552002%2C-80.8061065673828" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Haberdish"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/350.webp" alt="Map showing Haberdish" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
