                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>3106 N Davidson St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7048171084">(704) 817-1084</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The fried chicken is the order, and the collards are the side worth keeping. The room runs at volume on weekends, so a reservation is the practical move.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r24"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-korean-food-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-korean-food-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Korean Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Seoul Food Meat Company</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-pancakes-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/best-pancakes-charlotte-hero-300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Pancakes in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> The Flipside Cafe</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r25" data-rank="25" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Modern Setting|Upscale Dining|Local Favorite">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">25</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/ab/4c/7e/paella-and-steam-bun.jpg" alt="Sea Level NC" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Sea Level NC photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Sea Level NC</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Seafood &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.0 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.0</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Sea Level NC landed in First Ward as Charlotte was still figuring out what kind of food city it wanted to be.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Raw Oyster Selection</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Grouper</span><span class="pl">Lobster Roll</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7044122616">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2276867%2C-80.8413472" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Sea Level NC"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">NC Oysters and Coastal Focus in First Ward</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Raw Oyster Selection</b><p>The raw bar anchor at this Uptown seafood room, ordered as the table-setter before anything else arrives.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Grouper</b><p>Grouper is the kind of catch that shows whether a kitchen respects its fish; the pan-sear here is the test.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Lobster Roll</b><p>The lobster roll draws the kind of attention that keeps the menu honest about what a coastal-leaning room in the 704 is actually reaching for.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Sea Level NC landed in First Ward as Charlotte was still figuring out what kind of food city it wanted to be. The premise is straightforward: NC seafood, raw and cooked, in a room that reads upscale without demanding a special occasion to justify the tab. That positioning has held. The raw oyster selection is the anchor, and the kitchen treats it seriously, which matters in a landlocked banking city where the oyster program at most rooms is an afterthought.</p>
<p>The clam chowder has developed a reputation well beyond what a Charlotte seafood room might reasonably expect, the kind of dish that earns specific, unprompted return mentions. Pan-seared grouper and a lobster roll round out the menu as the cooked-seafood cases the kitchen makes for itself. The grouper in particular signals that the kitchen is not simply running a raw bar with a few obligatory entrees beside it. The lobster roll lands the room in a specific price-and-format conversation: moderately priced for what it is, which in Charlotte's Uptown means accessible to the after-work banking crowd without sliding into expense-account territory.</p>
<p>Service at Sea Level gets attention in the record, not as a generic pleasantry but as a specific asset, the kind of floor that moves the meal forward without pressure. The room skews date-night and celebration, which the coastal register supports, but the everyday bar program and the chowder suggest it handles a Tuesday just as well. Charlotte did not have a credible downtown seafood room for most of its modern dining history. Sea Level NC is the correction.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2276867%2C-80.8413472" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Sea Level NC"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/357.webp" alt="Map showing Sea Level NC" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
