            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 7.0 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>7.0</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Easy Like Sunday has settled into the kind of neighborhood brunch anchor Charlotte keeps producing as the city fills in its weekends.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Chicken and Waffles</span><span class="pl">Breakfast Skillet</span><span class="pl">Eggs Benedict</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9803352428">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.171992%2C-80.84832" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Easy Like Sunday"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Charlotte&#039;s Sunday Morning Ritual, Done Right</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Chicken and Waffles</b><p>The menu anchor at Easy Like Sunday, pairing fried chicken with waffles in the format that defines the room&#039;s identity.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Breakfast Skillet</b><p>A skillet-built morning plate that consolidates the kitchen&#039;s breakfast program into a single, hearty format.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Eggs Benedict</b><p>The hollandaise-topped brunch classic that draws a consistent crowd and reflects the kitchen&#039;s core eggs-and-protein approach.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Easy Like Sunday has settled into the kind of neighborhood brunch anchor Charlotte keeps producing as the city fills in its weekends. The room draws families and regulars who treat it less as an event and more as a reliable Saturday and Sunday institution, the kind of place that earns its waits rather than manufacturing them.</p>
<p>The chicken and waffles anchor the menu and give the kitchen its clearest identity statement: Southern-leaning comfort in a format the city's brunch culture has fully adopted as its own. The breakfast skillet works the same register, straightforward execution built for people who want something substantial without ceremony. Eggs Benedict rounds out the morning-to-midday range and reflects a kitchen operating in the standard brunch idiom rather than pushing outside it.</p>
<p>That honesty is worth stating plainly. The food here is competent and satisfying rather than ambitious. Eggs run soft, which not every diner will want, and the kitchen's seasoning choices on the sausage read as unconventional enough that first-timers may notice. This is a room whose appeal is consistency and hospitality, not the kind of cooking that repositions Charlotte on a culinary map.</p>
<p>What makes the room work is the service culture. The front of house runs with genuine warmth, and individual servers earn repeated mentions for going beyond the transactional. For a moderately priced brunch spot, that front-of-house investment matters as much as what comes off the line.</p>
<p>Waits are real, especially on weekends. What starts as a quoted 45-minute window can stretch considerably, and the room's popularity means first-come logistics apply. The price point is approachable, which explains a lot about who fills those seats: families, neighborhood regulars, and the rotating wave of newcomers the 704 produces every quarter.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.171992%2C-80.84832" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Easy Like Sunday"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/365.webp" alt="Map showing Easy Like Sunday" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
