      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r27"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-with-a-view-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/best-restaurants-with-a-view-charlotte-hero-300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants with a View in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Midwood Smokehouse</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-sandwiches-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-sandwiches-in-charlotte-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Sandwiches Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Lil Papi’s International Deli</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r28" data-rank="28" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">28</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-w/13/40/df/9c/let-s-meat-kbbq.jpg" alt="Let&#039;s Meat Kbbq" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Let&#039;s Meat Kbbq photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Let&#039;s Meat Kbbq</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Korean &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.9 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.9</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Let&#039;s Meat KBBQ holds a specific civic footnote: it opened as Charlotte&#039;s first all-you-can-eat Korean barbecue restaurant, which in a city still assembling its dining identity is a meaningful first.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Galbi Short Ribs</span><span class="pl">Bulgogi</span><span class="pl">Bibimbap</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9802994389">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2190478214665%2C-80.8576791733503" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Let&#039;s Meat Kbbq"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Charlotte&#039;s First All-You-Can-Eat Korean Table</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Galbi Short Ribs</b><p>The galbi short ribs anchor the all-you-can-eat program here, sweet-savory and meant for the tabletop grill.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Bulgogi</b><p>Bulgogi is the approachable entry point into the Korean BBQ rotation, thinly sliced and built for the grill.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Bibimbap</b><p>Bibimbap offers a cooked alternative to the tabletop format, a rice bowl that holds its own off the flame.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Let's Meat KBBQ holds a specific civic footnote: it opened as Charlotte's first all-you-can-eat Korean barbecue restaurant, which in a city still assembling its dining identity is a meaningful first. The format is interactive by design, built around tableside grills where diners cook their own galbi short ribs and bulgogi at their own pace, at a price point that lands in upscale territory for the genre. Bibimbap rounds out the anchor dishes, offering a composed alternative for anyone at the table who prefers a kitchen-finished plate over the grill.</p>
<p>The room reads as modern, not stripped-down, and the concept suits group dinners in a way that few Charlotte formats match. AYCE Korean barbecue is social infrastructure as much as it is a meal: the table shares the work, the ordering cycles through rounds, and the banchan that surrounds the grill provides the context for the proteins. The format also self-selects for a certain kind of visit, one oriented toward time spent together rather than a quick turn.</p>
<p>The honest picture is mixed. The galbi and bulgogi remain the reasons to go, and the AYCE structure rewards groups willing to move through multiple rounds. But the record includes real notes about execution inconsistency, with sides arriving watery or underseasoned, and the kitchen's calibration appears to vary by visit. Parking validation has also drawn complaints: the restaurant advertises it, but the process has not worked smoothly for everyone. Neither issue is fatal to the concept, but both are friction points worth knowing before a group makes the trip.</p>
<p>Charlotte's Korean dining options have grown alongside the city's broader demographic diversification, and an AYCE anchor in this format fills a gap the scene had. The room is best approached as exactly what it is: a high-energy group table, calibrated for the right occasion.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2190478214665%2C-80.8576791733503" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Let&#039;s Meat Kbbq"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/434.webp" alt="Map showing Let&#039;s Meat Kbbq" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
