        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">32</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/18/8e/92/50/pinky-s-westside-grill.jpg" alt="Pinky&#039;s Westside Grill" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Pinky&#039;s Westside Grill photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Pinky&#039;s Westside Grill</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Burgers &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.7 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.7</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Pinky&#039;s Westside Grill opened in 2010 in a former Volkswagen repair shop on West Morehead, and the bones of that build-out have served it well: a neighborhood burger joint with enough character to pull out-of-towners back on return visits to the 704.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pinky&#039;s Classic Burger</span><span class="pl">Buffalo Wings</span><span class="pl">Loaded Fries</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
