          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r32"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-tacos-charlotte-local-favorites/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-tacos-in-charlotte-6-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Tacos in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Sabor Latin Street Grill</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-japanese-food-charlotte/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-japanese-food-in-charlotte-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Japanese Restaurants in Charlotte (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> King Fish Poke</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r33" data-rank="33" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Casual Vibes|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">33</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/1a/3a/45/62/hawkers-interiors.jpg" alt="Hawkers Asian Street Food" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Hawkers Asian Street Food photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Hawkers Asian Street Food</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Asian Fusion &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.7 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.7</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Hawkers is an Orlando-based chain that landed in Charlotte riding the same transplant-driven appetite for casual, shareable Asian street food that has reshaped the city&#039;s mid-market dining over the past decade.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Roti Canai</span><span class="pl">Char Kway Teow</span><span class="pl">Vietnamese Pork Banh Mi</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7044640770">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.21109%2C-80.86105" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Hawkers Asian Street Food"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Pan-Asian Street Food, Charlotte&#039;s Banking-Boom Casual</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Roti Canai</b><p>A Malaysian flatbread that anchors the menu&#039;s Southeast Asian range, served with curry dipping sauce and worth ordering as the table gets settled.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Char Kway Teow</b><p>A Penang-style stir-fried rice noodle dish, the char and wok heat doing the work that makes this a credible version of the street-food original.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Vietnamese Pork Banh Mi</b><p>The Vietnamese-inflected sandwich pulls pork through the banh mi format, a useful entry point for the menu&#039;s broader Southeast and East Asian sweep.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Hawkers is an Orlando-based chain that landed in Charlotte riding the same transplant-driven appetite for casual, shareable Asian street food that has reshaped the city's mid-market dining over the past decade. The concept covers a lot of ground: Southeast Asian hawker-stall staples, Korean, Vietnamese, Hong Kong-style plates, and more, all under one roof at a moderately accessible price point. That breadth is the point.</p>
<p>The Roti Canai is the right place to start, a flaky, pull-apart flatbread that signals the Malaysian street-food register the room draws on. The Char Kway Teow, the wok-fried rice noodle dish that is a fixture of Penang and Singapore hawker centres, gives the menu its Southeast Asian spine. The Vietnamese Pork Banh Mi rounds out the range with the kind of clean, herb-forward build the sandwich demands.</p>
<p>Beyond those anchors, the Hong Kong Sticky Ribs read as a kitchen highlight: char siu-seasoned, glazed for sweetness, the kind of dish that holds its own against anything at a more specialized room. The kimchi, a side that could be an afterthought elsewhere, earns attention here. The Korean section of the menu is where regulars tend to return.</p>
<p>For Charlotte, the room functions as a reliable group table. The format suits the city's young-transplant dining culture: casual, order-several-things, nobody needs to navigate a specialist cuisine alone. Service is notably attentive for the format.</p>
<p>This is not the Central Avenue corridor's immigrant-run regional cooking. It is a polished multi-concept operation designed for accessibility, and it executes that program with consistency. For what it is, the kitchen delivers.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.21109%2C-80.86105" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Hawkers Asian Street Food"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/348.webp" alt="Map showing Hawkers Asian Street Food" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
