                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1930 Camden Rd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7044640770">(704) 464-0770</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The Hong Kong Sticky Ribs and the Korean dishes reward repeat visits; order both alongside the Roti Canai to cover the menu&#039;s strongest range. The room runs at volume on weekends, so arriving early keeps the wait short.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r33"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-belmont/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-belmont-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Belmont (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Nellie&#x27;s Southern Kitchen</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-mount-holly/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-mount-holly-9-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Mount Holly (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Samvay&#x27;s Wings &amp; Subs</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r34" data-rank="34" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Cozy Atmosphere">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">34</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/30/a0/e4/51/classic-italian-american.jpg" alt="Mama Ricotta&#039;s" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Mama Ricotta&#039;s photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Mama Ricotta&#039;s</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Italian &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.6 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.6</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Mama Ricotta&#039;s opened in August 1992 as Frank Scibelli&#039;s first restaurant, the seed of what became FS Food Group and one of the longer-running Italian rooms in the 704.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Chicken Parmigiana</span><span class="pl">Fettuccine Alfredo</span><span class="pl">Margherita Pizza</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/mama-ricottas/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043430148">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.20994181432107%2C-80.83565158546358" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Mama Ricotta&#039;s"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Frank Scibelli&#039;s Italian anchor, still running strong</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Chicken Parmigiana</b><p>The kitchen anchor at Frank Scibelli&#039;s first restaurant, open on Kings Drive since 1992, where the parmigiana stays classic and unapologetic.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Fettuccine Alfredo</b><p>A straightforward Alfredo that earns its place on a menu where the Italian-American standards are taken seriously and portions run generous.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Margherita Pizza</b><p>The margherita holds its own on a menu built around crowd-pleasing execution rather than novelty, a reliable read on the kitchen&#039;s baseline.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Mama Ricotta's opened in August 1992 as Frank Scibelli's first restaurant, the seed of what became FS Food Group and one of the longer-running Italian rooms in the 704. That longevity matters in Charlotte, where the independent dining scene is genuinely young and most anchors are measured in years, not decades. The restaurant sits on the moderately priced end of the spectrum, which partly explains its staying power through every wave of new openings the city has cycled through.</p>
<p>The kitchen runs a classic Italian-American program. Chicken Parmigiana is the kind of execution that builds a reputation over thirty-plus years: straightforward, consistent, and portioned generously enough that finishing is a commitment. The Fettuccine Alfredo holds the same lane, rich and uncomplicated. The Margherita Pizza is a cleaner, more restrained plate, a useful read on how the kitchen handles simplicity. The lasagna draws strong responses as well, the kind of dish that earns repeat visitors on its own.</p>
<p>Portions run large across the board, and the room operates with full table service at a pace that feels practiced rather than rushed. The FOH is attentive without being mechanical about it, the sort of service that rounds out a family dinner without anyone noticing the mechanics. Reservations are worth making; the room fills, especially on weekends, and the volume the kitchen handles at peak times speaks to how well the operation has been calibrated over time.</p>
<p>For a city that was largely chain territory as recently as the 1980s, a locally rooted Italian room that has held a lease this long and still draws crowds is a meaningful data point. Scibelli built something that outlasted the novelty of its opening, which in Charlotte's fast-cycling dining market is the real accomplishment.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.20994181432107%2C-80.83565158546358" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Mama Ricotta&#039;s"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/356.webp" alt="Map showing Mama Ricotta&#039;s" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Daily: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>601 S Kings Dr Aa</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043430148">(704) 343-0148</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Reservations are not optional on busy nights; the room books out and the wait reflects it. The lasagna is worth ordering alongside whatever else lands on the table.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r34"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-pineville/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-pineville-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Pineville (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Waldhorn Restaurant</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-mint-hill/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-mint-hill-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Mint Hill (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Dunwellz</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r35" data-rank="35" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Romantic Spot|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">35</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/18/ba/28/a1/20190810-213343-largejpg.jpg" alt="Luce" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Luce photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Luce</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Italian &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.5 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.5</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Luce sits in the Uptown orbit, the kind of room Charlotte&#039;s banking-era build-out keeps producing: polished, dim, and built for the expense-account occasion.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">House-made Pappardelle Bolognese</span><span class="pl">Wood-fired Margherita Pizza</span><span class="pl">Pan-seared Branzino</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/luce/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043449222">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.227999583065746%2C-80.84085183943425" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Luce"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Uptown Italian Where the Room Still Delivers</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>House-made Pappardelle Bolognese</b><p>The house-made pappardelle here is the plate that anchors Luce&#039;s kitchen, wide ribbons holding a slow-built Bolognese that earns its place on the menu.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Wood-fired Margherita Pizza</b><p>Wood-fired crust keeps the Margherita honest, the kind of straightforward measure of a kitchen&#039;s technique worth ordering at any Italian room.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Pan-seared Branzino</b><p>Branzino pan-seared whole or in fillet is the seafood anchor on the menu, a reliable read of how seriously Luce treats its fish program.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Luce sits in the Uptown orbit, the kind of room Charlotte's banking-era build-out keeps producing: polished, dim, and built for the expense-account occasion. The Italian program runs wider than a single signature, and the kitchen appears to take it seriously across the board.</p>
<p>The house-made pappardelle Bolognese is the anchor pasta, and the craftsmanship in hand-rolled pasta is the kind of detail that separates a real Italian room from a concept. The wood-fired Margherita pizza reads like a litmus test: a kitchen confident enough to let simple ingredients carry weight. The pan-seared branzino represents the seafood lane, and the execution holds up alongside the risotto specials, which have drawn real attention from the dining room.</p>
<p>The room runs dim and composed, which suits the pre-theater and special-occasion crowd that fills it. The proximity to the Belk Theater is not incidental. The service is calibrated to the pace of the evening: a table with a curtain time can move through a full dinner without the meal feeling abbreviated. That operational precision is harder to sustain than the menu itself, and when it lands, it is the room's most reliable asset.</p>
<p>The wine list supports an Italian kitchen at this price point, and the combination draws the kind of parties, business dinners, anniversaries, groups of women treating a weeknight like an event, that Uptown's dining corridor runs on. Charlotte did not have rooms like this in 1985. It has several now, and Luce earns its place among them.</p>
<p>At upscale pricing, the expectation is consistency across every visit. The kitchen clears that bar on the signature pastas and the fish. The service record is strong but not perfectly uniform, which is worth noting for a room positioning itself at the top of the market.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.227999583065746%2C-80.84085183943425" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Luce"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/590.webp" alt="Map showing Luce" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
