                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1800 E 7th St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043779017">(704) 377-9017</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The crawfish étouffée is the order to anchor a meal here. The live music schedule shapes the room&#039;s energy considerably, so an evening visit on a music night runs differently than a quieter seating.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
      <div class="gmb2" data-after="r36"><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-denver-nc/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-denver-nc-10-local-picks-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Denver (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Chillfire Bar &amp; Grill</em></span></a></div><div class="promotion-block promotion-guide" data-recommendation="You may also like"><span class="promotion-label">You may also like</span><a class="gmb" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/best-restaurants-harrisburg/"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/best-restaurants-in-harrisburg-10-local-favorites-2026--300x167.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" width="104" height="70"><span class="gmb-t"><b>Best Restaurants in Harrisburg (2026)</b><em><span class="n1">&#8470; 1:</span> Wake Up &amp; Eat</em></span></a></div></div>      <article class="lrow" id="r37" data-rank="37" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Romantic Spot|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">37</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/J2hHK2ECRE6YTOLBJA6rcw/l.jpg" alt="Oak Steakhouse" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/oak-steakhouse-charlotte?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Oak Steakhouse photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Oak Steakhouse</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Steakhouses &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.2 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.2</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Oak Steakhouse is the kind of room Charlotte&#039;s banking economy was always going to produce: polished, reservation-forward, built for the work dinner that needs to impress and the occasion that warrants the bill.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Dry-Aged Ribeye</span><span class="pl">Filet Mignon with Truffle Butter</span><span class="pl">Wagyu Beef Sliders</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/oak-steakhouse/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7049548900">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.14656796268216%2C-80.83127899995905" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Oak Steakhouse"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">The Expense-Account Steakhouse Charlotte Built For</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Dry-Aged Ribeye</b><p>The flagship cut here, dry-aged for depth of flavor and the kind of char-to-center contrast that defines the steakhouse program.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Filet Mignon with Truffle Butter</b><p>Filet Mignon arrives finished with truffle butter, the kitchen&#039;s answer to the banking-crowd expectation of polish on a lean cut.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Wagyu Beef Sliders</b><p>The Wagyu sliders read as an entry point to the beef program, a smaller-format way to assess the kitchen&#039;s sourcing priorities.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Oak Steakhouse is the kind of room Charlotte's banking economy was always going to produce: polished, reservation-forward, built for the work dinner that needs to impress and the occasion that warrants the bill. The city has been generating expense-account steakhouses since the banking boom took hold, and Oak sits squarely in that tradition, offering a full-service, upscale experience where the room itself signals intent before the food arrives.</p>
<p>The dry-aged ribeye is the anchor of the menu and the argument for coming. Dry-aging concentrates flavor in a way that separates a serious program from a steakhouse going through the motions, and the ribeye here carries that depth. The filet mignon, finished with truffle butter, reads as the menu's concession to the diner who wants refinement over chew, a leaner cut dressed for a special occasion. The wagyu beef sliders function as the entry point, the thing that works for a group grazing through a business dinner without committing to a full plate.</p>
<p>The room handles large parties and operates at volume on a Friday, with a bustling floor and a layout divided into multiple sections. Groups of eight get seated and fed without the wheels coming off, which is a real operational test for a high-end steakhouse and one Oak appears to pass. The drinks program holds up under scrutiny, relevant in a room where the bar tab often rivals the food.</p>
<p>Charlotte didn't have rooms like this in the 1980s. The city built them alongside the banking towers, one lease at a time, for a clientele that arrived with corporate cards and a need for somewhere that looked the part. Oak is that room, done with the seriousness the occasion demands.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.14656796268216%2C-80.83127899995905" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Oak Steakhouse"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/556.webp" alt="Map showing Oak Steakhouse" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 5:00 PM - 9:00 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 5:00 PM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 5:00 PM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>4777 Sharon Rd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7049548900">(704) 954-8900</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Book well ahead for groups; the room moves and fills. The dry-aged ribeye is the reason to come, not the sliders, though the sliders make sense if the table is splitting a business-dinner spread.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r38" data-rank="38" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Upscale Dining|Cozy Atmosphere">
