          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Customshop Handcrafted Food photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Customshop Handcrafted Food</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">New American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.0 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.0</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Customshop sits in the chef-driven tier that Charlotte spent the post-LYNX decade constructing, one serious kitchen at a time.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Halibut</span><span class="pl">Handcrafted Burger with House-Cut Fries</span><span class="pl">Seasonal Seafood Risotto</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/customshop-handcrafted-food/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043333396">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.21393%2C-80.82623" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Customshop Handcrafted Food"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">The Room Charlotte Built Its Standards On</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Halibut</b><p>The halibut anchors the savory side of the menu, a kitchen-focused preparation that reflects Customshop&#039;s handcrafted approach to proteins.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Handcrafted Burger with House-Cut Fries</b><p>The burger is the room&#039;s casual cornerstone, house-cut fries included, and holds its own against the more composed plates.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Seasonal Seafood Risotto</b><p>Risotto built around what is seasonal keeps this dish shifting with the calendar, making it the reliable gauge of where the kitchen&#039;s focus sits.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Customshop sits in the chef-driven tier that Charlotte spent the post-LYNX decade constructing, one serious kitchen at a time. The Michelin Guide named it Recommended in 2025, and the designation tracks: this is the kind of room that earns its standing through execution rather than concept novelty. The menu reads as tight and seasonal, the sort of short, focused program where each plate has a reason to exist. Pan-seared halibut is the flagship, and it signals what the kitchen is doing across the board: clean technique on good protein, no theatrical distractions.</p>
<p>The seasonal seafood risotto belongs in the same conversation, a dish that shifts with the calendar and rewards the kitchen for knowing when to leave something alone. The handcrafted burger with house-cut fries is the room's concession to accessibility, and it holds its own against the composed plates around it. Service runs at the level the food demands. The room handles large parties without losing its composure, and the front-of-house reads as genuinely attentive rather than performatively polished.</p>
<p>For a city whose upscale dining long skewed toward expense-account steakhouses and national concepts, a room like this one represents a different kind of ambition: independent, particular, grounded in craft. The price is upscale but not opaque; this is special-occasion territory for most, though the burger and the bar program give the room a bit more flexibility than the occasion framing suggests. Charlotte's dining identity is still being assembled, but Customshop is one of the rooms doing the assembling. The 2025 Michelin Recommended designation confirms what the kitchen has been arguing for years.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.21393%2C-80.82623" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Customshop Handcrafted Food"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/581.webp" alt="Map showing Customshop Handcrafted Food" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon: Closed</b><b>Tue - Sat: 5:00 PM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: Closed</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1601 Elizabeth Ave</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043333396">(704) 333-3396</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The pan-seared halibut is the clearest expression of what the kitchen does at its best. For larger groups, the room manages the logistics well, but booking ahead is the right call.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r39" data-rank="39" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Romantic Spot|Local Favorite">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">39</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/Pk9StuWYpg-KFM_LOqCFcw/l.jpg" alt="Stagioni Four Seasons of Food" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/stagioni-four-seasons-of-food-charlotte?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Stagioni Four Seasons of Food photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Stagioni Four Seasons of Food</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Italian &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.0 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.0</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Stagioni takes a full-season Italian program seriously in a Charlotte dining room built for expense-account occasion and deliberate date nights.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">House-made Pappardelle Bolognese</span><span class="pl">Osso Buco alla Milanese</span><span class="pl">Branzino in Crosta di Sale</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043728110">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.200325%2C-80.824611" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Stagioni Four Seasons of Food"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Seasonal Italian in the Uptown Banking Belt</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>House-made Pappardelle Bolognese</b><p>The kitchen&#039;s own pappardelle carries the bolognese well, with the pasta made in-house rather than sourced, the kind of detail that shapes how a braise lands.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Osso Buco alla Milanese</b><p>Osso buco alla Milanese is the room&#039;s most traditional anchor, a Milanese braise that takes its time and rewards accordingly.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Branzino in Crosta di Sale</b><p>Branzino baked in a salt crust is a classic Italian technique that seals in moisture and lets the fish speak plainly, the menu&#039;s quietest dish and often its most precise.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Stagioni takes a full-season Italian program seriously in a Charlotte dining room built for expense-account occasion and deliberate date nights. The name signals the kitchen's orientation: a menu that rotates with the calendar, drawing on classical northern Italian technique rather than the red-sauce shortcuts that fill most local Italian rooms. House-made pappardelle Bolognese is the throughline dish, the kind of long-braised ragu that earns its time on the menu; the wide ribbons hold the sauce the way dried pasta never quite manages. Osso Buco alla Milanese represents the special-occasion anchor of the program, a Milanese braise that takes hours and shows it, the marrow the finish that separates the kitchen from anything casual.</p>
<p>Branzino in crosta di sale is the lighter counterpoint, the salt-crust method a piece of European technique that keeps the fish honest without layering on distraction. Portions run on the smaller side, which suits the room's pace: courses arrive as a progression rather than a volume exercise, and the kitchen's precision reads in a restrained plate rather than a heaped one. Service is the variable. Attentive and fluent on a good night, the front of house can extend the meal into a genuinely considered experience; on a harder night, the hospitality register drops noticeably and the room loses its footing.</p>
<p>Charlotte's Italian landscape has widened since the banking boom brought serious restaurant investment Uptown and into SouthPark, but scratch-kitchen northern Italian at this price point is still a narrower lane. Stagioni aims at the higher end of that lane, and when the kitchen and the floor operate in concert, it holds the position.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.200325%2C-80.824611" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Stagioni Four Seasons of Food"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/555.webp" alt="Map showing Stagioni Four Seasons of Food" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon: 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM</b><b>Tue - Sat: 5:00 PM - 9:30 PM</b><b>Sun: Closed</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>715 Providence Rd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043728110">(704) 372-8110</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The pappardelle Bolognese is the order that justifies the kitchen&#039;s identity here; build the meal around it. The smaller portion format rewards ordering multiple courses rather than treating a single entree as the whole meal.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r40" data-rank="40" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Local Favorite|Romantic Spot">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">40</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/2a/55/4f/d6/the-asbury-dining-room.jpg" alt="The Asbury" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="The Asbury photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">The Asbury</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Southern &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 6.0 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>6.0</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">The Asbury sits in the theater district Uptown, positioned to catch pre-curtain diners headed to Belk Theatre and the surrounding stages.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Shrimp and Grits</span><span class="pl">Fried Chicken</span><span class="pl">Braised Short Ribs</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/the-asbury/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043421193">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.22875749097565%2C-80.84111885276414" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for The Asbury"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Southern Fare at the Theater District Address</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Shrimp and Grits</b><p>The Asbury&#039;s signature plate, shrimp and grits grounds the menu in new-Southern form steps from Belk Theatre in Uptown.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Fried Chicken</b><p>Fried chicken anchors the Southern side of a menu built for pre-theater diners who want a proper meal before the curtain.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Braised Short Ribs</b><p>Braised short ribs represent the heavier, slow-cooked register on a menu that moves between Southern staples and dining-room polish.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>The Asbury sits in the theater district Uptown, positioned to catch pre-curtain diners headed to Belk Theatre and the surrounding stages. That location is the room's clearest asset and, depending on the night, its clearest liability: it draws crowds on show evenings, and the kitchen runs under that pressure. The menu is Southern, anchored by shrimp and grits, fried chicken, and braised short ribs. These are dishes that reward a kitchen operating with care; the shrimp and grits in particular is the kind of plate that earns repeat visits when the execution holds. The short ribs carry the weight expected of an upscale Southern room, and the fried chicken gives the menu a foothold in the honest, unglamorous tradition Charlotte's new-Southern wave has largely built itself on.</p>
<p>Charlotte's upscale Southern category is not enormous; the room competes in a tier that expects more than a good location and a prix-fixe option. The prix-fixe format is available here, a sensible structure for a theater-crowd room where diners are watching the clock, but billing accuracy has been a friction point. That is the kind of operational detail that lands hard at upscale prices, where the expectation is that the back-of-house professionalism matches the front. The drinks program holds up as a straightforward complement to the food, without a particular distinction.</p>
<p>The room reads as a special-occasion address, a date-night choice for Uptown diners who want Southern cooking in a polished setting. At upscale pricing, the gap between the room's best nights and its inconsistent ones is noticeable. The concept is sound: Uptown, Southern, theater-adjacent, prix-fixe available. Whether a given evening delivers on that promise is less settled. Diners who have been before carry a reasonable sense of what to expect; first-timers should set expectations accordingly.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.22875749097565%2C-80.84111885276414" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to The Asbury"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/539.webp" alt="Map showing The Asbury" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 7:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b><b>Fri: 7:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sat: 8:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 8:00 AM - 8:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>235 N Tryon St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043421193">(704) 342-1193</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The shrimp and grits is the dish most consistently worth ordering here. If using the prix-fixe, confirm the total before the card goes down.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r41" data-rank="41" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Cozy Atmosphere|Upscale Dining">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">41</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/IqLaURriP2a6TMO0ToOSCQ/l.jpg" alt="The Goodyear House" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/the-goodyear-house-charlotte?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="The Goodyear House photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">The Goodyear House</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Tapas Bars &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 5.9 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>5.9</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">The Goodyear House sits in NoDa, the old Highland Park Mill neighborhood that traded textile money for tapas and brewery taprooms.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Chorizo and Manchego Board</span><span class="pl">Patatas Bravas</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Scallops</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/the-goodyear-house/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7049100132">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.245963%2C-80.807065" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for The Goodyear House"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">NoDa small plates with a Spanish spine</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Chorizo and Manchego Board</b><p>The cured-meat-and-cheese board anchors the tapas format here, pairing Spanish chorizo with manchego for a direct entry into the room&#039;s Iberian register.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Patatas Bravas</b><p>Fried potato cubes with bravas sauce are the spine of any serious tapas program, and this version draws steady repeat orders from the NoDa crowd.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Scallops</b><p>The pan-seared scallops represent the kitchen&#039;s higher-end reach within the small-plates format, a reliable marker of how far the 704&#039;s dining scene has traveled.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>The Goodyear House sits in NoDa, the old Highland Park Mill neighborhood that traded textile money for tapas and brewery taprooms. The room runs a small-plates format with a Spanish lean, and the menu holds together as a coherent program rather than a scattered one. The Chorizo and Manchego Board is the logical starting point: cured meat, aged cheese, a format that rewards sharing and sets the register for the rest of the meal. Patatas Bravas follow the same logic, the kind of dish that works as a table anchor while other plates rotate in. The Pan-Seared Scallops represent the kitchen stepping up in commitment, a protein that requires real timing discipline and which the menu uses to signal range beyond the charcuterie-and-snacks lane.</p>
<p>The room draws a crowd for date nights and small group gatherings, which fits the format: tapas pacing keeps the table occupied and gives a group somewhere to go. The drinks program is taken seriously, and the bar pulls its weight alongside the food rather than functioning as an afterthought. Tuesday evenings run at a pace that still feels alive without the weekend press, which makes the room accessible on off-peak nights.</p>
<p>NoDa is where Charlotte's independent dining scene put down its early roots, building on the mill-village bones the neighborhood kept after the looms went quiet. The Goodyear House occupies that context without leaning on it too heavily; it functions as a neighborhood anchor for residents of the area while drawing from across the 704 for the occasion. At an upscale price point, the expectation is execution that matches the format's ambition, and the kitchen's range across the menu suggests that ambition is grounded.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.245963%2C-80.807065" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to The Goodyear House"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/486.webp" alt="Map showing The Goodyear House" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Sat: 11:00 AM - 10:30 PM</b><b>Sun: 10:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>3032 N Davidson St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7049100132">(704) 910-0132</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The Chorizo and Manchego Board is the move to anchor the table; order early and build around it. Tuesday evenings offer a slower pace than the weekend without sacrificing the full program.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r42" data-rank="42" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Modern Setting|Local Favorite">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">42</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/e0/0e/06/elegance-and-fine-food.jpg" alt="Bernardin&#039;s Restaurant At Ratcliffe" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Bernardin&#039;s Restaurant At Ratcliffe photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Bernardin&#039;s Restaurant At Ratcliffe</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">New American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 5.7 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>5.7</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Bernardin&#039;s at Ratcliffe occupies the segment of the Charlotte dining map that the banking boom built and still sustains: upscale, full-service, suited to a business dinner or a milestone occasion.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Grouper</span><span class="pl">Dry-Aged Ribeye</span><span class="pl">Lobster Risotto</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/bernardins-restaurant-at-ratcliffe/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043323188">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2243605443209%2C-80.8469950971852" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Bernardin&#039;s Restaurant At Ratcliffe"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Expense-Account New American With Staying Power</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Grouper</b><p>The grouper anchors the seafood side of the menu, a pan-seared preparation where crispy skin and clean flavor are the benchmark.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Dry-Aged Ribeye</b><p>The dry-aged ribeye is the room&#039;s most serious red-meat commitment, the aging process concentrating flavor in a way that separates it from a standard steakhouse cut.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Lobster Risotto</b><p>Lobster risotto sits at the center of the New American program here, pairing a rich shellfish component with the kind of slow-built starch that defines the format.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Bernardin's at Ratcliffe occupies the segment of the Charlotte dining map that the banking boom built and still sustains: upscale, full-service, suited to a business dinner or a milestone occasion. The room runs at the polished end of the New American register, and the menu reflects that positioning across every course.</p>
<p>The pan-seared grouper is the kitchen's lightest statement, a fish preparation that depends on execution at the burner level for its texture and finish. The dry-aged ribeye is the room's power move, the kind of cut that signals to an expense-account table that the kitchen is playing in a specific tier. Dry-aging is a commitment in time and in margin, and the presence of it on the menu says something about where Bernardin's has positioned itself among Charlotte's upscale rooms. The lobster risotto rounds out the signature three as the mid-register indulgence, the dish that works for the guest who wants richness without the weight of a full steak.</p>
<p>Charlotte's upscale dining category is dominated by banking-money rooms, many of them national or regional concepts that arrived with the corporate build-out. A room like Bernardin's that holds a local identity in that tier is operating in genuine competition with well-capitalized national brands, and the loyal return business around the salmon preparation in particular suggests the kitchen has built some consistent habits worth noting.</p>
<p>The price point is what the market and the cut of meat require. Business diners and special-occasion tables are the natural audience. The room runs full service, and the reservation is the right call.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2243605443209%2C-80.8469950971852" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Bernardin&#039;s Restaurant At Ratcliffe"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/585.webp" alt="Map showing Bernardin&#039;s Restaurant At Ratcliffe" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:30 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Fri: 11:30 AM - 10:30 PM</b><b>Sat: 5:00 PM - 10:30 PM</b><b>Sun: Closed</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>435 S Tryon St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043323188">(704) 332-3188</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The salmon, ordered consistently by regulars, comes with crispy skin as its calling card; if the kitchen is running it well that evening, it is the lower-risk entry point over the heavier proteins. Reserve in advance for weekend occasions, and confirm hours before arriving late in the evening.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r43" data-rank="43" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Brunch Spot|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">43</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/51/2a/70/plenty-of-dishes.jpg" alt="Napa on Providence" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Napa on Providence photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Napa on Providence</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">New American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 5.6 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>5.6</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Charlotte&#039;s upscale dining story runs through two tracks: the expense-account rooms Uptown, and the neighborhood-anchored rooms that serve the city&#039;s residential corridors.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Salmon</span><span class="pl">Braised Short Ribs</span><span class="pl">Truffle Mac and Cheese</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/napa-on-providence/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7049008535">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.1968338367888%2C-80.8260918945122" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Napa on Providence"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Providence Road&#039;s Quiet Case for New American</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Salmon</b><p>The salmon anchors the lighter end of a New American menu that skews toward polished, occasion-ready plates.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Braised Short Ribs</b><p>Braised short ribs represent the kind of slow-cooked centerpiece that defines Napa on Providence&#039;s approach to comfort-meets-craft dining.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Truffle Mac and Cheese</b><p>Truffle mac and cheese works as either a standalone indulgence or the richest side on the table.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Charlotte's upscale dining story runs through two tracks: the expense-account rooms Uptown, and the neighborhood-anchored rooms that serve the city's residential corridors. Napa on Providence occupies the second lane, a New American room on Providence Road that works the date-night and special-occasion calendar without the Uptown address or the Uptown price floor.</p>
<p>The kitchen leads with three signatures that announce its ambitions plainly. Pan-seared salmon is a reliable test of execution consistency, and this room passes it with enough regularity to anchor the menu. Braised short ribs represent the heavier end of the program, slow-cooked protein that rewards a full-service room willing to take its time. Truffle mac and cheese arrives as either a side or a main depending on the appetite, and its presence signals a kitchen that understands its crowd: Charlotte's new-resident population that wants familiar comfort dressed for a nicer occasion.</p>
<p>The room operates on reservations and takes them seriously. Tables at the 8 PM hour fill, and the bar runs its own program independent of the dining room. Happy hour, available Sunday through Thursday, makes the bar an accessible entry point on nights when the dining room feels like a commitment. The bar seat also draws visitors and short-timers, people passing through the Myers Park corridor who want something more composed than a hotel lobby pour.</p>
<p>The Charlotte context matters here. The city did not have a dining scene to speak of thirty years ago; rooms like this one represent the residential dining infrastructure that followed the banking boom into the city's southern neighborhoods. Napa on Providence is not a Michelin conversation, but it is a working neighborhood anchor doing the quieter work of building a full-service culture in the 704.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.1968338367888%2C-80.8260918945122" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Napa on Providence"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/485.webp" alt="Map showing Napa on Providence" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:30 AM - 9:30 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 11:30 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 10:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>110 Perrin Pl</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7049008535">(704) 900-8535</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The bar program runs happy-hour specials Sunday through Thursday with both food and drink pricing; the charcuterie board makes a reasonable opening move before moving to the dining room or settling in for the evening.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r44" data-rank="44" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Modern Setting|Local Favorite">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">44</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-w/23/87/c2/63/check-this-out.jpg" alt="Deluxe Fun Dining" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Deluxe Fun Dining photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Deluxe Fun Dining</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Bars &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 5.6 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>5.6</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Deluxe Fun Dining positions itself at the intersection of polished cooking and a room that does not take itself too seriously, and the menu makes good on that premise.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Pan-Seared Duck Breast</span><span class="pl">Truffle Mac and Cheese</span><span class="pl">Bourbon-Glazed Pork Tenderloin</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/deluxe-fun-dining/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9803322220">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.228139%2C-80.846605" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Deluxe Fun Dining"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Upscale Charlotte Room That Plays Its Name Straight</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Pan-Seared Duck Breast</b><p>The pan-seared duck breast anchors the savory side of a menu that plays between bar energy and full-plate ambition.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Truffle Mac and Cheese</b><p>Truffle mac and cheese lands as the room&#039;s comfort centerpiece, the kind of side that tends to outshine the table.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Bourbon-Glazed Pork Tenderloin</b><p>The bourbon-glazed pork tenderloin reads as the menu&#039;s straightforward crowd-pleaser, sweet-savory and built for the Deluxe atmosphere.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Deluxe Fun Dining positions itself at the intersection of polished cooking and a room that does not take itself too seriously, and the menu makes good on that premise. The signature dishes read like a kitchen with real technique behind them: pan-seared duck breast, a bourbon-glazed pork tenderloin, and truffle mac and cheese. That last item is the tell. A kitchen confident enough to put truffle mac on an upscale menu alongside duck is betting that its guests want comfort and craft in the same sitting, and the menu bears that out. The lobster and red velvet waffle that the room has become known for pushes the same logic further, pairing a luxury shellfish with something that belongs on a Sunday brunch table.</p>
<p>It should not work as a fine-dining proposition, and yet that combination lands consistently enough to have become a signature. The drinks program is clearly part of the draw here, not an afterthought. Charlotte's post-LYNX dining boom produced plenty of rooms where the cocktail list functions as the real product, and Deluxe operates in that tradition, with the food pulling equal weight. The service model is full-service table service, attentive enough to support a date-night or a celebration without the stiffness of an expense-account steakhouse. At an upscale price point, Deluxe lands in the tier of Charlotte rooms where the occasion is part of what is being sold.</p>
<p>The energy in the room leans toward celebratory rather than hushed, which separates it from the SouthPark dining-as-transaction register. The kitchen is executing a short list of strong dishes at a price that reflects the ambition. For Charlotte's younger, occasion-minded dining crowd, that is a legitimate position to hold.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.228139%2C-80.846605" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Deluxe Fun Dining"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/430.webp" alt="Map showing Deluxe Fun Dining" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 4:30 PM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Fri: 4:30 PM - 12:00 AM</b><b>Sat: 10:30 AM - 12:00 AM</b><b>Sun: 10:30 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>305 W 4th St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:9803322220">(980) 332-2220</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The lobster and red velvet waffle is the move. Arrive with a reservation on weekend evenings; the room runs at volume and the wait without one can be substantial.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r45" data-rank="45" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Outdoor Seating">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">45</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/1a/37/b1/f1/private-room-available.jpg" alt="Cabo Fish Taco" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Cabo Fish Taco photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Cabo Fish Taco</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Latin American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 5.5 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>5.5</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Cabo Fish Taco opened in NoDa in 2002, which in Charlotte restaurant years makes it something close to ancient.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Beer-Battered Fish Tacos</span><span class="pl">Carne Asada Burrito</span><span class="pl">Street Corn Elote</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/cabo-fish-taco/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043328868">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.24724%2C-80.80587" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Cabo Fish Taco"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">NoDa&#039;s Original Fish Taco Room, Still Standing</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Beer-Battered Fish Tacos</b><p>The anchor order at this NoDa room, beer-battered fish tacos have anchored Cabo&#039;s menu since the place opened in 2002.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Carne Asada Burrito</b><p>Carne asada gets the burrito treatment here, a straightforward choice for those who want something more substantial than tacos.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Street Corn Elote</b><p>Street corn elote rounds out an order and reflects the Latin street-food sensibility the room has built its reputation on.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Cabo Fish Taco opened in NoDa in 2002, which in Charlotte restaurant years makes it something close to ancient. The neighborhood has cycled through several identities since then, the breweries arrived, the light rail changed the economics of the corridor, and Cabo has held its lease through all of it. That longevity is the first thing worth noting.</p>
<p>The room runs casual and loud. Thursday evenings draw a packed house, the kind of crowd that fills seats early and keeps the noise level up through the night. Seating is plentiful, the patio extends the footprint, and the whole operation moves at the pace of a neighborhood spot that has figured out its rhythm over two decades of service.</p>
<p>The beer-battered fish tacos are the anchor of the menu and the reason the place built its reputation. The batter is the point: the technique produces a crust that holds against the toppings without going heavy, and the fish itself reads as the honest center of the plate rather than a delivery vehicle for sauce. Street corn elote rounds out the table well, the kind of side that signals a kitchen paying attention to the Latin American pantry beyond the taco. The carne asada burrito handles the heavier end of the menu, straightforward and filling, the thing to order when the tacos feel too light for the occasion.</p>
<p>The price sits in the moderate range, which is consistent with what NoDa's casual corridor has always done best: honest food at a number that does not require a banking-sector expense account. For a city that spent the 1980s relying on chains to fill this role, a place like Cabo represents exactly the kind of independent room Charlotte has been building toward, one lease at a time, since the scene started to develop.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.24724%2C-80.80587" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Cabo Fish Taco"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/352.webp" alt="Map showing Cabo Fish Taco" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 11:00 AM - 11:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>3201 N Davidson St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043328868">(704) 332-8868</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The beer-battered fish tacos are the order; the street corn elote alongside them covers the table. Thursday evenings run full, so expect noise and a wait for seating.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
