          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/cabo-fish-taco-ballantyne-charlotte?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Cabo Fish Taco - Ballantyne photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Cabo Fish Taco - Ballantyne</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Latin American &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 5.4 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>5.4</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Cabo Fish Taco planted its original flag in NoDa in 2002, and the Ballantyne location carries that same fish-taco-and-margaritas register into Charlotte&#039;s southern suburban corridor.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Baja Fish Tacos</span><span class="pl">Loaded Nachos Supreme</span><span class="pl">Tableside Guacamole</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/cabo-fish-taco-ballantyne/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:9803352869">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.06058947279322%2C-80.83851764470126" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Cabo Fish Taco - Ballantyne"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Ballantyne&#039;s Beach-Casual Taco Anchor</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Baja Fish Tacos</b><p>The signature order at this Latin American cantina, built around beer-battered white fish in warm tortillas with the slaw and crema the menu is known for.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Loaded Nachos Supreme</b><p>Loaded nachos that function as a table-anchor, the kind of shareable that defines the visit before the tacos arrive.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Tableside Guacamole</b><p>Mixed tableside, which means the guacamole is as fresh as guacamole gets and lets the table control heat and texture from the start.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Cabo Fish Taco planted its original flag in NoDa in 2002, and the Ballantyne location carries that same fish-taco-and-margaritas register into Charlotte's southern suburban corridor. The room runs casual and family-forward, which fits Ballantyne's demographic squarely: this is weeknight dinner territory and happy-hour territory, not an expense-account room.</p>
<p>The Baja Fish Tacos are the anchor order and the reason the kitchen has sustained repeat business across years. The preparation follows the Baja template honestly: battered fish, slaw, crema, the acidic cut that makes the format work. Regulars who return after long gaps report the food holds its level, which is a meaningful consistency signal for a moderately priced multi-location concept.</p>
<p>The Loaded Nachos Supreme and Tableside Guacamole fill out the shareable end of the menu. The guacamole, prepared at the table, is the kind of interactive element that earns goodwill at a casual family dinner; it also does the honest work of anchoring the Latin American frame beyond tacos. The nachos run large and operate as a group dish.</p>
<p>The room itself is a split proposition. The back and the patio are the better seats; the interior can read cramped in the tighter sections, and the outdoor space is the clear preference when the weather cooperates. In Charlotte's long spring-through-fall window, the patio is a real asset.</p>
<p>The chips and salsa arrive as a table standard, though temperature inconsistency has come up as a variable. Service has ranged from enthusiastic and helpful to merely functional depending on the shift. At a moderately priced spot in the southern suburbs, the floor staff tends to carry the experience when the kitchen is doing its job reliably in the background.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.06058947279322%2C-80.83851764470126" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Cabo Fish Taco - Ballantyne"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/562.webp" alt="Map showing Cabo Fish Taco - Ballantyne" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>11611 N Community House Rd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:9803352869">(980) 335-2869</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The patio is the seat to request; the interior back section is the fallback if the outdoor space is full. The Baja Fish Tacos are the throughline order that holds up across visits.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r47" data-rank="47" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$" data-tags="Local Favorite|Family Friendly|Casual Vibes">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">47</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/Gvv5I8s2xpJPYtzD4m3aBw/l.jpg" alt="Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/merts-heart-and-soul-charlotte?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Southern &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 4.8 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>4.8</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul has held a lease in First Ward since 1998, which makes it a long-running institution by any measure in a city where the independent dining scene is genuinely young.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Fried Chicken</span><span class="pl">Mac and Cheese</span><span class="pl">Buttermilk Biscuits with Sausage Gravy</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
                        <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043424222">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.227442491372734%2C-80.8404245576721" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Soul Food Anchor in the First Ward</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Fried Chicken</b><p>The anchor of the Uptown soul food room that James Bazzelle opened in 1998, straightforward Southern fried chicken done without apology.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Mac and Cheese</b><p>A side that earns its own reputation here, rich enough to hold its own against the heavier plates on the menu.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Buttermilk Biscuits with Sausage Gravy</b><p>The breakfast-inflected opener that signals Mert&#039;s commitment to the soul food canon, biscuit and gravy as a Southern baseline.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Mert's Heart &amp; Soul has held a lease in First Ward since 1998, which makes it a long-running institution by any measure in a city where the independent dining scene is genuinely young. The room is small, fills fast, and the kitchen runs at volume, that combination means most waits are short but the place rarely feels empty. It is the kind of room that earns its regulars on the strength of a focused, consistent menu rather than on novelty.</p>
<p>The fried chicken is the center of gravity here: straightforward, properly executed, the kind of thing that explains why the room built its reputation on Southern comfort cooking rather than on reinvention. Mac and cheese runs alongside it as a natural companion, carrying enough weight to hold up as a reason to visit on its own. The buttermilk biscuits with sausage gravy cover the breakfast-and-brunch side of the equation and suggest a kitchen that takes the supporting cast as seriously as the headliners.</p>
<p>The soul rolls are the sleeper order: collard greens and pinto beans rolled and fried, a format that gives the kitchen's Southern vocabulary a different texture and a sharper edge than the plate-style sides. That dish shows up repeatedly as the thing that surprises first-time visitors who arrive expecting nothing but straightforward plate lunches.</p>
<p>Charlotte's Southern dining options have grown considerably since the 2010s, with rooms like Haberdish and Leah and Louise staking out new-Southern and juke-joint territory. Mert's operates in an older register: Lowcountry and soul, no chef-driven framing, no small-plates architecture. For the city's lunch and brunch crowd that wants a filling, moderately priced plate in Uptown without the expense-account overhead, that positioning still has a clear purpose. The room is for families, for midday breaks from the office towers nearby, and for anyone who wants to eat well without a reservation.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.227442491372734%2C-80.8404245576721" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/355.webp" alt="Map showing Mert&#039;s Heart &amp; Soul" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>214 N College St</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043424222">(704) 342-4222</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The soul rolls are the move at Mert&#039;s: order them before the main plate. The room fills fast at peak lunch hours, so arriving early or slightly off-peak keeps the wait minimal.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r48" data-rank="48" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Family Friendly|Modern Setting|Sports Bar">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">48</span>
                    <img src="https://s3-media0.fl.yelpcdn.com/bphoto/egSI4smg_upsLQlKRMYfMQ/l.jpg" alt="Topgolf" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz/topgolf-charlotte?adjust_creative=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw&#038;utm_campaign=yelp_api_v3&#038;utm_medium=api_v3_business_search&#038;utm_source=ncSIOsUpFaM6ZuPenKQYtw" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Topgolf photo on Yelp"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/yelp-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Yelp"></a></span>
                            </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Topgolf</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Golf &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 4.3 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>4.3</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Topgolf is not a restaurant that happens to have golf; it is an entertainment venue that happens to serve food, and the distinction matters when setting expectations.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Nashville Hot Chicken Sandwich</span><span class="pl">Loaded Mac and Cheese</span><span class="pl">Craft Burgers</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/topgolf/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7046124745">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.153539%2C-80.9449111" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Topgolf"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Golf Bays, Bar Food, Group Energy</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Nashville Hot Chicken Sandwich</b><p>The spice-forward sandwich anchors the casual American menu, bringing heat-driven Nashville-style chicken to a sports-entertainment room built around the bays.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Loaded Mac and Cheese</b><p>Mac and cheese loaded with toppings does the work of a shareable plate between swings, fitting the group-dining rhythm of the space.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Craft Burgers</b><p>The burger lineup covers the reliable center of the menu when the group splits between golf and food.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Topgolf is not a restaurant that happens to have golf; it is an entertainment venue that happens to serve food, and the distinction matters when setting expectations. The format is straightforward: covered, climate-controlled bays where groups hit tracked golf balls at targets while servers work the floor. The room runs on group bookings and walk-ins looking for a shared activity, and the floor moves at the pace of an occupied sports bar rather than a conventional dining room.</p>
<p>The food sits in upscale-casual territory for a concept where eating is secondary to the experience. The Nashville Hot Chicken Sandwich draws attention as the kitchen's sharpest item, landing the heat level and the structural contrast that makes the format work. Craft burgers hold up as reliable centerpieces for a table that wants something substantial between rounds. The Loaded Mac and Cheese functions well as a shared plate, the kind of dish that travels easily across a group without debate.</p>
<p>Not everything on the menu performs at the same level. The jalapeno popper dip arrives inconsistently, and the chips alongside it have drawn complaints about texture. The drinks program is where the room earns its upscale price point most convincingly: cocktails come out strong and well-made, and bar service reads as attentive throughout the night. Pizza has surfaced as a practical group option, serviceable and easy to share across a bay.</p>
<p>Charlotte's entertainment dining category has grown alongside the city's transplant population, and Topgolf lands squarely in the banking-crowd and corporate-outing segment: upscale pricing, polished service, a format that works for colleagues and visitors alike. The heaters keep the bays usable through the cooler months, which extends the useful season for after-work groups. For a city still building its independent dining identity, this is the national-concept entertainment end of the spectrum, and it fills that lane without apology.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.153539%2C-80.9449111" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Topgolf"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/451.webp" alt="Map showing Topgolf" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 10:00 AM - 11:00 PM</b><b>Fri: 10:00 AM - 1:00 AM</b><b>Sat: 9:00 AM - 1:00 AM</b><b>Sun: 9:00 AM - 12:00 AM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>8024 Savoy Corporate Dr</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7046124745">(704) 612-4745</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">Stick to the Nashville Hot Chicken Sandwich and the craft burgers as the most consistent food orders; the drinks program is the real draw, so budget accordingly and let the bartenders work.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
            <article class="lrow" id="r49" data-rank="49" data-hood="Charlotte" data-price="$$$" data-tags="Upscale Dining|Romantic Spot|Modern Setting">
        <div class="restaurant-overview">
        <div class="lr-ph">
          <span class="lr-no">49</span>
                    <img src="https://media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-m/1280/19/7a/82/9c/dry-aged-long-bone-ribeye.jpg" alt="Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450" decoding="async">
          <span class="lr-cred"><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" aria-label="Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse photo on Tripadvisor"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/plugins/custom-business-directory/assets/images/tripadvisor-logo-dark-bg.svg" alt="Tripadvisor"></a></span>                  </div>
        <div class="lr-main">
          <div class="lr-hd">
            <div class="lr-tt">
              <h3 class="lr-name">Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse</h3>
              <span class="lr-meta">Steakhouses &middot; Charlotte &middot; <span class="bb-pr">$$$</span></span>
            </div>
            <span class="lr-score" aria-label="Insider Score 4.3 out of 10"><span>Insider Score</span><b>4.3</b></span>          </div>
          <p class="lr-hook">Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse is the kind of room Charlotte&#039;s expense-account economy was built to support: polished, consistent, and calibrated for the business dinner or the anniversary that needs to go right.</p>          <span class="lr-order"><span class="u-lbl">What to order</span><span class="pl">Filet Mignon</span><span class="pl">Lobster Mac and Cheese</span><span class="pl">Chocolate Soufflé</span></span>          <span class="lr-cta">
            <a class="u-btn primary" href="https://topofcharlotte.com/go/book/sullivans-steakhouse/?z=board" rel="nofollow">Restaurant Reservations</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="tel:7043358228">Call</a>            <a class="u-btn secondary" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2101676933474%2C-80.8599308916656" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Directions</a>
          </span>
                  </div>
        </div>
                <details class="review-details">
          <summary aria-label="Review and visiting details for Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse"><span class="when-closed">Read the full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="when-open">Full review &amp; visiting details</span><span class="detail-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="lr-fold">
          <div class="lf-body">
            <h4 class="lf-hd2">Banking-money steakhouse, twenty years running</h4>                        <div class="lf-dishes">
              <div class="fd"><b>Filet Mignon</b><p>The menu anchor at this SouthPark-area steakhouse, the filet is the cut that keeps long-running regulars on a two-decade rotation.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Lobster Mac and Cheese</b><p>A rich side that crosses into main-event territory, the lobster mac earns consistent attention from tables splitting courses.</p></div><div class="fd"><b>Chocolate Soufflé</b><p>The soufflé requires patience but lands as the natural close to a full steakhouse evening here.</p></div>            </div>
                        <div class="lf-prose"><p>Sullivan's Steakhouse is the kind of room Charlotte's expense-account economy was built to support: polished, consistent, and calibrated for the business dinner or the anniversary that needs to go right. The filet mignon is the anchor of the menu, the reliable signature that has kept tables coming back across two decades of the city's banking-boom growth. It reads as the sort of kitchen that treats the center-cut well and doesn't overcomplicate it. The lobster mac and cheese works as a steakhouse side should, a rich counterweight that earns its price on the check.</p>
<p>The chocolate soufflé is the dessert to plan around, the kind of finish that requires patience at the table and rewards it. That combination of steak, indulgent sides, and a proper dessert program is the steakhouse formula done at upscale price points, and Sullivan's has held that lane in Charlotte long enough to mean something in a city where most of the dining scene is young. Charlotte's steakhouse culture runs on banking money and the Uptown corridor, and a room that has operated continuously for over twenty years here has outlasted the build-out cycles and the concept churn that reshaped the city after the LYNX line arrived. The room skews toward special occasions and business entertaining, with the polish of full table service and an interior that signals occasion without announcing itself.</p>
<p>This is not the independent-chef side of Charlotte's food story; it is the expense-account side, and it plays that role honestly. For the Mecklenburg visitor or the transplant with a client dinner, Sullivan's is a known quantity in the best sense of that phrase.</p>
</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lf-rail">
                        <a class="lf-map" href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&#038;destination=35.2101676933474%2C-80.8599308916656" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" aria-label="Directions to Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse"><img src="https://topofcharlotte.com/wp-content/uploads/rowmaps/442.webp" alt="Map showing Sullivan&#039;s Steakhouse" loading="lazy" width="300" height="200"><span class="osm">&copy; OpenStreetMap</span></a>
                        <div class="lf-rows">
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Hours</i><b>Mon - Thu: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b><b>Fri - Sat: 11:00 AM - 11:00 PM</b><b>Sun: 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM</b></div>
                            <div class="lf-row"><i>Address</i><b>1928 S Blvd</b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Phone</i><b><a href="tel:7043358228">(704) 335-8228</a></b></div>              <div class="lf-row"><i>Insider tip</i><p class="tiptext">The filet mignon is the standard-bearer here; order it and let the lobster mac and cheese do its job alongside. The chocolate soufflé requires advance notice at the table, so plan for it at the start of the meal.</p></div>            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        </details>
              </article>
          </div>
