  <!-- FAQ (visible; feeds the FAQPage schema above) -->
  <section class="faqp">
    <div class="k sig">The method</div>
    <h2>About this ranking</h2>
    <div class="qagrid">
        <div class="qa"><h3>How is this ranking calculated?</h3><p>Every restaurant earns an Insider Score from 0 to 10, built from its full review record and weighted for review volume, recency, and our editors' read. The same method is applied to every kitchen in Charlotte.</p></div>
        <div class="qa"><h3>What is the best restaurant in Charlotte right now?</h3><p>Curry Gate 2 holds the top spot on this week's List with an Insider Score of 8.1. The kitchen serves Indian, at 5516 South Blvd.</p></div>
        <div class="qa"><h3>Which Charlotte neighborhoods have the most restaurants on the List?</h3><p>Concord leads this week with 2 ranked rooms, followed by Matthews with 1 and Fort Mill with 1.</p></div>
        <div class="qa"><h3>How often is the list updated?</h3><p>It is rebuilt every week from the current review record, so a room that slips or surges moves with the numbers.</p></div>
        <div class="qa"><h3>Why do lesser-known restaurants rank so high?</h3><p>Because the data puts them there. The score does not know where a restaurant sits. A neighborhood counter and a marquee dining room are measured exactly the same way.</p></div>
        </div>
  </section>

  
